<text x="340" y="295" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d4d5ca" font-size="13">Age at injury (years)</text><text x="13" y="145" transform="rotate(-90 13 145)" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d4d5ca" font-size="12">Change in points / 36</text></svg>
<p class="chart-note">Age versus scoring change: <strong>r ≈ −0.11</strong>, a very weak negative relationship. Players <strong>under 30</strong> (15 players) averaged a <strong>2.4-point decline</strong>, while players <strong>over 30</strong> (5 players) averaged a <strong>4.1-point decline</strong>. The four players aged exactly 30 were kept separate, averaging a 2.3-point decline. Haliburton, at 25, falls in the under-30 group.</p></div>
<p>That might sound encouraging for Haliburton, but there was plenty of variation even among younger players. Age alone isn't enough to tell us how he'll return.</p>
<div class="chart"><h3>03 / Height and scoring change</h3><small>Each dot is one historical player · change in points per 36 after return</small><svg class="scatter" viewBox="0 0 690 300" role="img" aria-label="Height (inches) versus scoring change">
{[-10,-5,0,5].map(t=><g><line x1="58" y1={245-(t+11)/16*190} x2="625" y2={245-(t+11)/16*190} stroke={t===0?"#d4ff45":"#45483e"} stroke-dasharray={t===0?"5 5":"2 6"}/><text x="48" y={249-(t+11)/16*190} text-anchor="end" fill="#b8b9af" font-size="12">{t>0?"+":""}{t}</text></g>)}
{[73,77,81,84].map(t=><text x={58+(t-72)/13*565} y="270" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b8b9af" font-size="12">{t}</text>)}
{players.map(p=><circle cx={58+(p.height-72)/13*565} cy={245-(p.post-p.pre+11)/16*190} r="5.5" fill="#d4ff45" opacity=".85"><title>{p.name}: {p.height}, {(p.post-p.pre).toFixed(1)} points/36</title></circle>)}
<line x1="275.3076923076923" x2="275.3076923076923" y1="22" y2="245" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-dasharray="4 5" opacity=".75"/>
<text x="340" y="295" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d4d5ca" font-size="13">Height (inches)</text><text x="13" y="145" transform="rotate(-90 13 145)" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d4d5ca" font-size="12">Change in points / 36</text></svg><p class="chart-note">Pearson correlation: <strong>r ≈ −0.25</strong>. Dashed vertical line marks Haliburton's height. At 77 inches (6 ft 5 in), Haliburton sits toward the shorter end of this sample. The weak negative correlation suggests taller players tended to lose somewhat more scoring production here, but height overlaps with position and playing style.</p></div>
<div class="chart"><h3>04 / Weight and scoring change</h3><small>Each dot is one historical player · change in points per 36 after return</small><svg class="scatter" viewBox="0 0 690 300" role="img" aria-label="Weight (pounds) versus scoring change">
{[-10,-5,0,5].map(t=><g><line x1="58" y1={245-(t+11)/16*190} x2="625" y2={245-(t+11)/16*190} stroke={t===0?"#d4ff45":"#45483e"} stroke-dasharray={t===0?"5 5":"2 6"}/><text x="48" y={249-(t+11)/16*190} text-anchor="end" fill="#b8b9af" font-size="12">{t>0?"+":""}{t}</text></g>)}
{[150,185,220,260].map(t=><text x={58+(t-145)/135*565} y="270" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b8b9af" font-size="12">{t}</text>)}
